flowchart TB
    accTitle: Password changes, security findings and Trash
    accDescr: Password changes retain at most ten prior values and update the password-change date; unrelated edits do not reset password age. Local Security Check returns secret-free weak, reused and at-least-365-days-old findings. Individual deletion moves an item to encrypted Trash, while restore, explicit permanent deletion, normal-unlock retention purge and confirmed group deletion have distinct outcomes. Older backups and snapshots are unaffected.
    subgraph editFlow["Edit and check a password"]
        edit{"Edit result?"}
        edit -->|New password| change["Keep up to 10 previous values\nSet password-change date"]
        edit -->|Other fields| metadata["Update item metadata\nKeep password age"]
        change --> saved[["Paired encrypted save"]]
        metadata --> saved
        saved --> check["Local Security Check\nActive nonempty passwords only"]
        check --> findings["Weak / exact reuse / age >= 365 days\nResults contain no password values"]
        findings --> fix["Open finding's ID in protected editor\nSave and rescan"]
    end
    subgraph deleteFlow["Delete or restore data"]
        removeRoute{"Deletion route?"}
        removeRoute -->|One item| trash["Move to encrypted Trash\nHide from normal list and autofill"]
        trash -->|Restore| restore["Clear deletion state\nPaired encrypted save"]
        trash -->|Delete permanently| gone["Remove from current vault\nPaired encrypted save"]
        trash -->|30 days; next normal unlock| gone
        removeRoute -->|Whole group + exact phrase| group["Remove group and all its items\nIncludes that group's Trash"]
        group --> gone
    end
